d byte-range slice\n  - `make_utf8_char_iter` / `next_utf8_char` — iterator producing one UTF-8 character per call\n  - `nth_utf8_char` — O(n) zero-based character lookup\n  - `utf8_char_count` — character count via the iterator\n  - `unicode_code_point` — bit-shift decoding for 1- to 4-byte forms\n- No `unsafe`, no FFI, no external crates added — pure safe Rust.\n- `cargo build` succeeds (only pre-existing warnings in `src/bin/test_utf8.rs` which is read-only).\n- `cargo test` reports 24 / 25 tests passing; the single failure is the test-translation issue described above."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":539,"cache_read_input_tokens":52257,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":539,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":41,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2afee55f-96d3-48b1-ad9a-7ceb71caf84a","uuid":"3147ab0c-230b-486f-ae84-e4abb847c61f"}
